.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.claude/
fonts/
*:Zone.Identifier
.vercel

# node deps (puppeteer-core install for hand exports)
node_modules/
# large / generated export artifacts — regenerate with scratch_folder/capture_frames.mjs
*.mov
scratch_folder/frames/

# Rendered video masters. `*.mov` alone was not enough: the fill/key delivery path
# (scratch_folder/export_fillkey.py) emits DNxHR-in-MXF, and a `git add -A` here
# would have staged 1.8GB across 46 files — every one over GitHub's 100MB limit,
# so the push fails *after* the objects are in local history and needs a rewrite
# to undo. All of it is regenerable from the SVG masters; none of it belongs in git.
*.mxf
exports/
scratch_folder/mxf-hive-test/

# Personal resume bookmark (save-point skill) — not project docs
SAVE-POINT.md

# Stray local artefacts — one-off experiment output and a screenshot, kept on
# disk for reference but not part of the app. Nothing here is needed to run,
# build or understand the tool.
samples/
Screenshot*.png

# Pilot outputs with the licensed Knowledge woffs inlined as data: URIs.
# fonts/ is ignored above to keep those files out of this public repo; these
# are the same bytes in base64, so they must be ignored too. Regenerate with
# scratch_folder/pilot_line_charts.py (tracked — it reads fonts/ at build time).
#
# Widened 2026-07-23: the old rules were name-specific (EDITED_chart*,
# EDITED_camera_*, ...), so any new hand-animation output under a different
# name would have been tracked — and carried the font bytes into a public
# repo. Match the whole class instead.
scratch_folder/EDITED_*.svg
scratch_folder/*_preview.html
scratch_folder/*_artifact.html
